.TH HU_CHANNEL 3 "" "helios-unix" "Library functions"
.SH NAME
hu_channel \- create a bounded native stream between tasks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <helios/unix/channel.h>
int hu_channel(int fds[2]);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a unidirectional stream backed by the native /fifo service.
fds[0] is the read endpoint and fds[1] the write endpoint. The buffer holds
16 KiB; backpressure applies when it fills. Use one producer and one consumer.
This is not a claim of POSIX pipe or PIPE_BUF atomic-write semantics.
.PP
Endpoints can be inherited using hu_spawn descriptor actions even across
processors. Communicating tasks use native messages, not TCP sockets.
Close unused endpoints in both tasks: a retained writer prevents the reader
from seeing EOF after the buffer drains. Handle partial reads and writes.
.SH EXAMPLE
To feed a child's standard input, create a channel, adddup2 its read end to
descriptor 0, and use closefrom=3 to discard extra inherited descriptors.
After successful spawning, close the parent's read end. Write through its
write end, close it to signal EOF, and reap the child. On launch failure,
close both endpoints. If an original endpoint is below 3, explicitly close
unused standard-descriptor copies without closing the final redirected fd.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; -1 with errno set on failure. Both output slots are initialized
to -1 before creation. EINVAL indicates NULL fds; ENOENT can indicate that
/fifo is unavailable. Creation and endpoint-open errors are also reported.
.SH SEE ALSO
hu_spawn(3), hu_poll(3), hu_resolve(3)
